{"name":"Flan","hex":"#f6e3b4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flan","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A baked tart with a sweet or savoury filling in an open-topped pastry case.","A dessert of congealed custard, often topped with caramel, especially popular in Spanish-speaking countries."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To splay or bevel internally, as a window-pane."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crème caramel","blocks":[{"text":"Crème caramel, crème renversée, caramel pudding, condensed milk pudding, or caramel custard is a custard dessert with a layer of clear caramel sauce. Some popular variants of this dish are called flan in Spanish-speaking countries, in the US, and in parts of southeast Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Cremecaramel.jpg/330px-Cremecaramel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cr%C3%A8me_caramel"},{"title":"Flan (British cuisine)","blocks":[{"text":"A flan, in British cuisine, is an egg-based dish with an open, rimmed pastry or sponge base containing a sweet or savoury filling. Examples are bacon and egg flan and custard tart."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Flan_2.jpg/330px-Flan_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flan_(British_cuisine)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Flan_con_nata.jpg/500px-Flan_con_nata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/Flan_con_nata.jpg/500px-Flan_con_nata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Restaurant-prepared order of crème caramel, with sauce and garnish","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlan_con_nata